{#
  Temperature runaway guard (hetero-rework integration spec §3.10).

  Atom loss already aborts LAMMPS; a configuration that blows up while keeping
  every atom does not, and spends its whole step budget before anyone reads the
  log. `fix halt` ends the run the first time the global temperature crosses
  `settings.simulation.halt_temperature_factor` x the target.

  `error hard` on purpose, matching the atom-loss behaviour: a runaway means
  the setup is wrong, so the remaining sweep arms would burn budget on the same
  fault. Nothing is written half-finished -- LAMMPS exits before write_data.

  `halt_temperature` is None when the guard is off, and the macro then emits
  nothing at all.
#}
{% macro emit_temperature_halt(halt_temperature) %}
{% if halt_temperature is not none and halt_temperature %}
# --- runaway-temperature guard ----------------------------------------------
variable        halt_T equal temp
fix             halt_hot all halt 1000 v_halt_T > {{ halt_temperature }} error hard message yes
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
